    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-19T21:17:31+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-19T21:17:31+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:47:31Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:47:31Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over NSW will extend a ridge westwards over SA during Saturday. A cold front will approach from the west late Saturday then move across SA on Sunday. Another high pressure system will move eastwards across waters to the south during Monday then over Victoria and the Tasman Sea on Tuesday. This high will extend a ridge westwards over SA ahead of a low pressure trough that is expected to move over the far west of SA during Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW011" description="Eastern Eyre Peninsula" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-19T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds northerly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds northerly 25 to 35 km/h increasing to 30 to 45 km/h before dawn then shifting southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the late morning and early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:00am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the morning then tending south to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 11 with daytime temperatures reaching between 16 and 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-22T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-21T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light during the morning then becoming east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-23T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-24T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-22T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-23T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Light winds becoming north to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending east to northeasterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
